#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:1
msgid "Part V: Zero-Allocation Engineering in Rust"
msgstr "Teil V: Allokationsfreie Technik in Rust"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:4
msgid ""
"We follow a connection from accept to response through one fixed buffer, "
"and examine the concurrent data structures that let many connection "
"threads share state without heap allocation on the request path. Where "
"memory safety would otherwise need machinery of its own (reader counts, "
"arenas, descriptor tables, teardown chains), we show how Rust ownership "
"provides it instead."
msgstr ""
"Wir verfolgen eine Verbindung vom Annehmen bis zur Antwort durch einen "
"einzigen festen Puffer und untersuchen die nebenläufigen Datenstrukturen, "
"mit denen viele Verbindungsthreads Zustand teilen, ohne auf dem "
"Anfragepfad Heap-Speicher zu allokieren. Wo Speichersicherheit sonst "
"eigene Mechanismen bräuchte (Leserzähler, Arenen, Deskriptortabellen, "
"Abbauketten), zeigen wir, wie Rusts Ownership sie stattdessen liefert."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:6
msgid "The Connection Loop"
msgstr "Die Verbindungsschleife"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:9 ../../zero-allocation.rst:388
msgid "Objectives"
msgstr "Lernziele"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:11
msgid ""
"By the end of this chapter, we should be able to explain how one 64 KiB "
"buffer serves an entire keep-alive connection, how the head and body are "
"located without copying, why every connection gets its own bounded "
"thread, how the proxy learns the origin's framing so a proxied client "
"connection can stay open, and which of these guarantees the borrow "
"checker proves for us."
msgstr ""
"Am Ende dieses Kapitels sollten wir erklären können, wie ein einziger "
"64-KiB-Puffer eine ganze Keep-alive-Verbindung bedient, wie Kopf und Body "
"ohne Kopieren gefunden werden, warum jede Verbindung einen eigenen "
"begrenzten Thread erhält, wie der Proxy die Rahmung des Ursprungsservers "
"erfährt, damit eine weitergeleitete Clientverbindung offen bleiben kann, "
"und welche dieser Garantien der Borrow-Checker für uns beweist."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:13
msgid "One Thread per Connection, Bounded"
msgstr "Ein Thread pro Verbindung, begrenzt"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:16
msgid ""
"Accept workers (``--workers``, one per CPU by default, at most 64) share "
"the listening socket. Each accepted connection is handed to a thread of "
"its own with a one-megabyte stack, and the accept loop goes straight back "
"to ``accept``. A thread that finishes its connection parks and takes the "
"next one, because creating and ending a thread for every connection "
"stalled the other threads (Part VIII, SID 0002). The alternative, serving "
"a connection to completion on the accept thread, was the first design: it "
"measured well on a single client and badly on sixty-four, because sixty "
"of them waited for a worker to finish its 256-request quota, and the tail "
"latency grew with every waiting client. With a thread per connection, the "
"p99 at 64 connections stays under one millisecond in every whole-product "
"workload, from 305 us to 857 us "
"(``benchmarks/results/product-latest.md``; Part VIII)."
msgstr ""
"Accept-Worker (``--workers``, standardmäßig einer pro CPU, höchstens 64) "
"teilen sich den lauschenden Socket. Jede angenommene Verbindung wird einem "
"eigenen Thread mit einem Stack von einem Megabyte übergeben, und die "
"Accept-Schleife kehrt sofort zu ``accept`` zurück. Ein Thread, der seine "
"Verbindung beendet hat, wartet geparkt und übernimmt die nächste, weil das "
"Erzeugen und Beenden eines Threads für jede Verbindung die anderen Threads "
"ins Stocken brachte (Teil VIII, SID 0002). Die Alternative, eine Verbindung "
"auf dem Accept-Thread bis zum Ende zu bedienen, war der erste Entwurf: Mit "
"einem einzelnen Client maß er gut und mit vierundsechzig schlecht, weil "
"sechzig von ihnen warteten, bis ein Worker sein Kontingent von 256 Anfragen "
"abgearbeitet hatte, und die Latenz am Verteilungsende mit jedem wartenden "
"Client wuchs. Mit einem Thread pro Verbindung bleibt das p99 bei 64 "
"Verbindungen in jeder Arbeitslast des Gesamtprodukts unter einer "
"Millisekunde, zwischen 305 µs und 857 µs "
"(``benchmarks/results/product-latest.md``; Teil VIII)."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:18
msgid ""
"The number of connection threads is bounded by ``--max-connections`` "
"(1,024 by default, at most 8,192). Past the bound the accept loop answers "
"``503 Service Unavailable`` on the new socket and closes it without "
"spawning anything, and counts the event in ``sibuna_overloaded_total``."
msgstr ""
"Die Zahl der Verbindungsthreads ist durch ``--max-connections`` begrenzt "
"(standardmäßig 1.024, höchstens 8.192). Jenseits der Grenze antwortet die "
"Accept-Schleife auf dem neuen Socket mit ``503 Service Unavailable`` und "
"schließt ihn, ohne etwas zu starten, und zählt das Ereignis in "
"``sibuna_overloaded_total``."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:20
msgid "Implementation: ``accept_loop``"
msgstr "Implementierung: ``accept_loop``"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:22
msgid ""
"Accepts connections, checks each against the connection bound, and "
"launches it on a thread of its own from the task pool. In "
"``cmd/sibuna/src/server.rs`` (crate ``sibuna``)."
msgstr ""
"Nimmt Verbindungen an, prüft jede gegen die Verbindungsgrenze und startet "
"sie auf einem eigenen Thread aus dem Task-Pool. In "
"``cmd/sibuna/src/server.rs`` (Crate ``sibuna``)."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:24
msgid ""
"fn accept_loop(server: &Arc<Server>, listener: &TcpListener) {\n"
"    while !server.is_stopping() {\n"
"        let stream = match listener.accept() {\n"
"            Ok((stream, _)) => stream,\n"
"            // ... out of descriptors or memory: back off 1 ms instead of "
"spinning\n"
"        };\n"
"        let limit = server.max_connections.load(Ordering::Relaxed);\n"
"        if server.connections.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed) >= limit {\n"
"            server.connections.fetch_sub(1, Ordering::Relaxed);\n"
"            server.metrics.overloaded.bump();\n"
"            let text = \"Service Unavailable: connection limit "
"reached\";\n"
"            reject(server, &stream, text);\n"
"            continue;\n"
"        }\n"
"        set_no_delay(&stream);\n"
"        let task_server = Arc::clone(server);\n"
"        let launched = server.tasks.launch(move || {\n"
"            let _counted = Counted(&task_server);\n"
"            crate::connection::serve(&task_server, &stream);\n"
"        });\n"
"        // ... a launch failure gives the place back and counts an "
"overload\n"
"    }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"fn accept_loop(server: &Arc<Server>, listener: &TcpListener) {\n"
"    while !server.is_stopping() {\n"
"        let stream = match listener.accept() {\n"
"            Ok((stream, _)) => stream,\n"
"            // ... Deskriptoren oder Speicher erschöpft: 1 ms warten statt "
"spinnen\n"
"        };\n"
"        let limit = server.max_connections.load(Ordering::Relaxed);\n"
"        if server.connections.fetch_add(1, Ordering::Relaxed) >= limit {\n"
"            server.connections.fetch_sub(1, Ordering::Relaxed);\n"
"            server.metrics.overloaded.bump();\n"
"            let text = \"Service Unavailable: connection limit reached\";\n"
"            reject(server, &stream, text);\n"
"            continue;\n"
"        }\n"
"        set_no_delay(&stream);\n"
"        let task_server = Arc::clone(server);\n"
"        let launched = server.tasks.launch(move || {\n"
"            let _counted = Counted(&task_server);\n"
"            crate::connection::serve(&task_server, &stream);\n"
"        });\n"
"        // ... scheitert der Start: Platz zurückgeben und Überlastung "
"zählen\n"
"    }\n"
"}"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:50
msgid ""
"``Counted`` is a guard whose ``Drop`` gives the connection's place in the "
"bound back however the thread ends, by return or by panic. The ``503`` "
"path drains what the client has already sent before it shuts down its "
"side of the socket: closing a socket over unread bytes answers with a "
"reset, and the reset would discard the ``503``."
msgstr ""
"``Counted`` ist ein Guard, dessen ``Drop`` den Platz der Verbindung "
"innerhalb der Grenze zurückgibt, wie auch immer der Thread endet, durch "
"Rückkehr oder durch Panic. Der ``503``-Pfad liest zuerst ab, was der "
"Client bereits gesendet hat, bevor er seine Seite des Sockets schließt: "
"Ein Socket, der über ungelesenen Bytes geschlossen wird, antwortet mit "
"einem Reset, und der Reset würde die ``503`` verwerfen."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:52
msgid ""
"Threads come from a ``TaskPool`` (``cmd/sibuna/src/tasks.rs``), a fixed "
"table of joinable slots. A finished thread keeps its stack until it is "
"joined, so a slot is joined when it is taken again, and a new task takes "
"the *lowest* finished slot rather than advancing a cursor. A cursor would "
"reach a finished slot again only after a full lap of the table, leaving "
"thousands of finished threads resident, and memory would grow with the "
"connections served instead of the connections open. A second guard, "
"``Finished``, marks the slot free when the task ends, so a panicking "
"connection frees its slot too."
msgstr ""
"Threads stammen aus einem ``TaskPool`` (``cmd/sibuna/src/tasks.rs``), "
"einer festen Tabelle joinbarer Slots. Ein beendeter Thread behält seinen "
"Stack, bis er gejoint wird. Daher wird ein Slot gejoint, wenn er erneut "
"belegt wird, und eine neue Aufgabe nimmt den *niedrigsten* beendeten "
"Slot, statt einen Cursor weiterzuschieben. Ein Cursor würde einen "
"beendeten Slot erst nach einer vollen Runde durch die Tabelle wieder "
"erreichen, sodass Tausende beendeter Threads resident blieben, und der "
"Speicher würde mit den bedienten Verbindungen wachsen statt mit den "
"offenen. Ein zweiter Guard, ``Finished``, markiert den Slot als frei, "
"wenn die Aufgabe endet, sodass auch eine Verbindung mit Panic ihren Slot "
"freigibt."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:54
msgid ""
"Memory is bounded the same way. A connection thread holds its 64 KiB read "
"buffer and 16 KiB write buffer on its stack, and a 40 KiB proxy workspace "
"on the heap, allocated once when the connection starts. The worst case is "
"therefore a known number rather than a function of how many sockets a "
"client can open. The idle reaper (below) closes connections that stop "
"sending, so a slow client cannot pin a thread past ``--idle-timeout``."
msgstr ""
"Der Speicher ist auf dieselbe Weise begrenzt. Ein Verbindungsthread hält "
"seinen 64-KiB-Lesepuffer und seinen 16-KiB-Schreibpuffer auf seinem Stack "
"und einen 40-KiB-Proxy-Arbeitsbereich auf dem Heap, der einmal beim Start "
"der Verbindung allokiert wird. Der schlechteste Fall ist daher eine "
"bekannte Zahl und keine Funktion davon, wie viele Sockets ein Client öffnen "
"kann. Der Idle-Reaper (siehe unten) schließt Verbindungen, die nichts mehr "
"senden, sodass ein langsamer Client einen Thread nicht über "
"``--idle-timeout`` hinaus festhalten kann."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:56
msgid "One Buffer per Connection"
msgstr "Ein Puffer pro Verbindung"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:59
msgid ""
"Every dynamic allocation on a request path is a denial-of-service lever: "
"fragmentation over days, allocator lock contention across threads, and "
"amplification by attackers who craft requests that maximise allocation. "
"Sibuna's rule is absolute: classification, verification, and proxy "
"hand-off run with zero heap allocation. The connection handler owns a 64 "
"KiB read buffer and a 16 KiB write buffer for the life of the socket; "
"everything else is a slice into them."
msgstr ""
"Jede dynamische Allokation auf einem Anfragepfad ist ein Hebel für Denial "
"of Service: Fragmentierung über Tage, Konkurrenz um die Sperre des "
"Allokators zwischen Threads und Verstärkung durch Angreifer, die Anfragen "
"so gestalten, dass sie die Allokation maximieren. Sibunas Regel ist "
"absolut: Klassifikation, Verifikation und Übergabe an den Proxy laufen "
"ohne jede Heap-Allokation. Der Verbindungshandler besitzt für die "
"Lebensdauer des Sockets einen 64-KiB-Lesepuffer und einen "
"16-KiB-Schreibpuffer; alles andere ist ein Slice in diese Puffer."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:61
msgid "Implementation: ``connection::serve``"
msgstr "Implementierung: ``connection::serve``"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:63
msgid ""
"Registers the connection with the idle reaper, sets up the buffers, the "
"proxy workspace and the engine cache once, and serves up to 4,096 "
"requests. In ``cmd/sibuna/src/connection.rs`` (crate ``sibuna``)."
msgstr ""
"Meldet die Verbindung beim Idle-Reaper an, richtet die Puffer, den "
"Proxy-Arbeitsbereich und den Engine-Cache einmal ein und bedient bis zu "
"4.096 Anfragen. In ``cmd/sibuna/src/connection.rs`` (Crate ``sibuna``)."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:65
msgid ""
"pub fn serve(server: &Server, stream: &TcpStream) {\n"
"    let Some(lease) = server.idle.register(stream) else { return };\n"
"    // ...\n"
"    let mut read_buffer = [0u8; MAX_REQUEST_BYTES]; // 64 KiB\n"
"    let mut write_buffer = [0u8; WRITE_BUFFER]; // 16 KiB\n"
"    let mut reader = Reader::new(stream, &mut read_buffer[..]);\n"
"    let mut peer = PeerText::default();\n"
"    peer.format(stream.peer_addr().ok());\n"
"    let mut link = Link {\n"
"        server,\n"
"        stream,\n"
"        writer: Writer::new(stream, &mut write_buffer[..]),\n"
"        workspace: Workspace::new(),\n"
"        cache: EngineCache::new(),\n"
"        activity: lease.activity(),\n"
"        last: false,\n"
"    };\n"
"    for served in 0..MAX_REQUESTS_PER_CONNECTION {\n"
"        link.last = served + 1 == MAX_REQUESTS_PER_CONNECTION;\n"
"        if !serve_one(&mut reader, &mut link, peer.as_bytes()) {\n"
"            break;\n"
"        }\n"
"        lease.touch();\n"
"    }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"pub fn serve(server: &Server, stream: &TcpStream) {\n"
"    let Some(lease) = server.idle.register(stream) else { return };\n"
"    // ...\n"
"    let mut read_buffer = [0u8; MAX_REQUEST_BYTES]; // 64 KiB\n"
"    let mut write_buffer = [0u8; WRITE_BUFFER]; // 16 KiB\n"
"    let mut reader = Reader::new(stream, &mut read_buffer[..]);\n"
"    let mut peer = PeerText::default();\n"
"    peer.format(stream.peer_addr().ok());\n"
"    let mut link = Link {\n"
"        server,\n"
"        stream,\n"
"        writer: Writer::new(stream, &mut write_buffer[..]),\n"
"        workspace: Workspace::new(),\n"
"        cache: EngineCache::new(),\n"
"        activity: lease.activity(),\n"
"        last: false,\n"
"    };\n"
"    for served in 0..MAX_REQUESTS_PER_CONNECTION {\n"
"        link.last = served + 1 == MAX_REQUESTS_PER_CONNECTION;\n"
"        if !serve_one(&mut reader, &mut link, peer.as_bytes()) {\n"
"            break;\n"
"        }\n"
"        lease.touch();\n"
"    }\n"
"}"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:93
msgid ""
"``read_head`` fills the buffer until the blank line appears, searching "
"only the bytes that arrived since the last search, and refuses heads over "
"16 KiB with ``431``. ``parse_request`` (crate ``sibuna-http``) produces a "
"``Request<'a>`` whose method, path, query, headers, and cookies are "
"slices of the buffer. The declared body is filled up to what fits and "
"sliced after the head. Then ``reader.consume(head_len + body_len)`` "
"advances the reader, so the next keep-alive request starts cleanly; the "
"reader moves the unread bytes to the front only when it needs room. A "
"chunked body is decoded in place behind the head (SID 0009): each step's "
"framing is cut out of the buffer, so the decoded prefix stays contiguous "
"for inspection. Internal routes are length-delimited and keep the "
"connection open. Proxied requests keep it open too, provided the origin's "
"response is framed and the body was fully buffered; the next sections "
"show how the proxy decides."
msgstr ""
"``read_head`` füllt den Puffer, bis die Leerzeile erscheint, durchsucht "
"dabei nur die seit der letzten Suche eingetroffenen Bytes und weist Köpfe "
"über 16 KiB mit ``431`` ab. ``parse_request`` (Crate ``sibuna-http``) "
"erzeugt einen ``Request<'a>``, dessen Methode, Pfad, Query, Header und "
"Cookies Slices des Puffers sind. Der angegebene Body wird gefüllt, soweit "
"er passt, und hinter dem Kopf als Slice genommen. Dann rückt "
"``reader.consume(head_len + body_len)`` den Leser vor, sodass die nächste "
"Keep-alive-Anfrage sauber beginnt; der Leser schiebt die ungelesenen "
"Bytes nur dann nach vorn, wenn er Platz braucht. Ein Chunked-Body wird an "
"Ort und Stelle hinter dem Kopf dekodiert (SID 0009): Die Rahmung jedes "
"Schritts wird aus dem Puffer herausgeschnitten, sodass das dekodierte "
"Präfix für die Prüfung zusammenhängend bleibt. Interne Routen sind "
"längenbegrenzt und halten die Verbindung offen. Weitergeleitete Anfragen "
"halten sie ebenfalls offen, sofern die Antwort des Ursprungsservers "
"gerahmt ist und der Body vollständig gepuffert wurde; die nächsten "
"Abschnitte zeigen, wie der Proxy entscheidet."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:96
msgid ""
"reader.buffered(): the unread window of the 64 KiB read buffer\n"
"+-------------------------+---------------------------+------------------------+\n"
"| request head            | body prefix               | pending           "
"     |\n"
"| at most 16 KiB, ends in | min(declared, room left), | the next request, "
"or   |\n"
"| CR LF CR LF             | chunked: decoded in place | the rest of an "
"upload  |\n"
"+-------------------------+---------------------------+------------------------+\n"
"|<------ head_len ------->|<-------- body_len ------->|\n"
"  ^ method, path, query,     ^ request.body              ^ ctx.pending "
"(the\n"
"    headers, cookies                                       proxy sends it "
"first)\n"
"\n"
"after the response: reader.consume(head_len + body_len)"
msgstr ""
"reader.buffered(): das ungelesene Fenster des 64-KiB-Lesepuffers\n"
"+-------------------------+---------------------------+------------------------+\n"
"| Anfragekopf             | Body-Präfix               | ausstehend          "
"   |\n"
"| höchstens 16 KiB, endet | min(declared, Restplatz), | nächste Anfrage "
"oder   |\n"
"| auf CR LF CR LF         | chunked: direkt dekodiert | Rest eines Uploads  "
"   |\n"
"+-------------------------+---------------------------+------------------------+\n"
"|<------ head_len ------->|<-------- body_len ------->|\n"
"  ^ Methode, Pfad, Query,   ^ request.body              ^ ctx.pending (der\n"
"    Header, Cookies                                       Proxy sendet es "
"zuerst)\n"
"\n"
"nach der Antwort: reader.consume(head_len + body_len)"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:96
msgid ""
"The connection's read buffer while one request is served. Every field of "
"the request is a slice of it."
msgstr ""
"Der Lesepuffer der Verbindung, während eine Anfrage bedient wird. Jedes "
"Feld der Anfrage ist ein Slice davon."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:110
msgid ""
"fn serve_one<W: Write>(\n"
"    reader: &mut Reader<'_, &TcpStream>,\n"
"    link: &mut Link<'_, W>,\n"
"    peer: &[u8],\n"
") -> bool {\n"
"    let head_len = match read_head(reader) {\n"
"        Head::Complete(length) => length,\n"
"        Head::TooLarge => { /* 431 \"Request head exceeds 16 KB\" */ "
"return false; }\n"
"        Head::Closed | Head::Failed => return false,\n"
"    };\n"
"    let framing = {\n"
"        let bytes = reader.buffered();\n"
"        let head = bytes.get(..head_len).unwrap_or_default();\n"
"        let request = match parse_request(head) {\n"
"            Ok(request) => request,\n"
"            Err(error) => return reject_head(link, error),\n"
"        };\n"
"        let declared = request.content_length().unwrap_or(0);\n"
"        // ... Expect: 100-continue\n"
"        if declared == 0 && !request.chunked {\n"
"            let upload = Upload::declared(&request);\n"
"            let pending = bytes.get(head_len..).unwrap_or_default();\n"
"            let keep = dispatch(link, request, pending, upload, 0, "
"peer);\n"
"            reader.consume(head_len);\n"
"            return keep;\n"
"        }\n"
"        (declared, request.chunked)\n"
"    };\n"
"    serve_with_body(reader, link, peer, head_len, framing)\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"fn serve_one<W: Write>(\n"
"    reader: &mut Reader<'_, &TcpStream>,\n"
"    link: &mut Link<'_, W>,\n"
"    peer: &[u8],\n"
") -> bool {\n"
"    let head_len = match read_head(reader) {\n"
"        Head::Complete(length) => length,\n"
"        Head::TooLarge => { /* 431 \"Request head exceeds 16 KB\" */ return "
"false; }\n"
"        Head::Closed | Head::Failed => return false,\n"
"    };\n"
"    let framing = {\n"
"        let bytes = reader.buffered();\n"
"        let head = bytes.get(..head_len).unwrap_or_default();\n"
"        let request = match parse_request(head) {\n"
"            Ok(request) => request,\n"
"            Err(error) => return reject_head(link, error),\n"
"        };\n"
"        let declared = request.content_length().unwrap_or(0);\n"
"        // ... Expect: 100-continue\n"
"        if declared == 0 && !request.chunked {\n"
"            let upload = Upload::declared(&request);\n"
"            let pending = bytes.get(head_len..).unwrap_or_default();\n"
"            let keep = dispatch(link, request, pending, upload, 0, peer);\n"
"            reader.consume(head_len);\n"
"            return keep;\n"
"        }\n"
"        (declared, request.chunked)\n"
"    };\n"
"    serve_with_body(reader, link, peer, head_len, framing)\n"
"}"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:143
msgid "What the borrow checker proves"
msgstr "Was der Borrow-Checker beweist"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:145
msgid ""
"The request slices stay valid only until the next fill of the buffer. "
"Sibuna states that rule as a type, not as a comment: the request is a "
"``Request<'a>``, and ``'a`` is a shared borrow of the reader's buffer. "
"Filling or consuming the buffer needs ``&mut reader``, which the compiler "
"refuses while a ``Request`` borrowed from it is still in use. In "
"``serve_one`` the request is moved into ``dispatch``, and only after that "
"call returns may ``reader.consume`` run; writing them the other way round "
"does not compile."
msgstr ""
"Die Slices der Anfrage bleiben nur bis zum nächsten Füllen des Puffers "
"gültig. Sibuna formuliert diese Regel als Typ, nicht als Kommentar: Die "
"Anfrage ist ein ``Request<'a>``, und ``'a`` ist eine geteilte Ausleihe "
"des Leserpuffers. Den Puffer zu füllen oder zu verbrauchen erfordert "
"``&mut reader``, was der Compiler verweigert, solange ein davon "
"geliehener ``Request`` noch verwendet wird. In ``serve_one`` wird die "
"Anfrage in ``dispatch`` verschoben, und erst nachdem dieser Aufruf "
"zurückgekehrt ist, darf ``reader.consume`` laufen; in umgekehrter "
"Reihenfolge geschrieben, kompiliert der Code nicht."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:147
msgid ""
"The same rule explains two choices that look odd at first. First, "
"``serve_with_body`` parses the head a second time. The first parse must "
"end its borrow before the body is buffered, because buffering a chunked "
"body moves bytes inside the buffer; the second parse borrows the settled "
"buffer. Parsing is deterministic and takes about 133 ns for a browser "
"request with a cookie (``zero_copy_request_and_cookie``, 132.5 ns, in "
"``benchmarks/results/primitives-latest.md``), so the second parse costs "
"little and yields the same verdict. Second, the proxy borrows the parsed "
"request and the pending bytes and must not refill the connection buffer, "
"so it reads further client bytes into an upload buffer of its own. "
"Because it cannot hand back what it read, the client connection is kept "
"only when the body was fully buffered."
msgstr ""
"Dieselbe Regel erklärt zwei Entscheidungen, die zunächst seltsam "
"aussehen. Erstens parst ``serve_with_body`` den Kopf ein zweites Mal. Der "
"erste Parse muss seine Ausleihe beenden, bevor der Body gepuffert wird, "
"weil das Puffern eines Chunked-Bodys Bytes innerhalb des Puffers "
"verschiebt; der zweite Parse leiht den zur Ruhe gekommenen Puffer. Das "
"Parsen ist deterministisch und dauert für eine Browseranfrage mit Cookie "
"etwa 133 ns (``zero_copy_request_and_cookie``, 132,5 ns, in "
"``benchmarks/results/primitives-latest.md``), daher kostet der zweite "
"Parse wenig und liefert dasselbe Urteil. Zweitens leiht der Proxy die "
"geparste Anfrage und die ausstehenden Bytes und darf den "
"Verbindungspuffer nicht neu füllen; deshalb liest er weitere Client-Bytes "
"in einen eigenen Upload-Puffer. Weil er Gelesenes nicht zurückgeben kann, "
"wird die Clientverbindung nur dann behalten, wenn der Body vollständig "
"gepuffert wurde."

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:149
msgid "The Proxy Head Rewrite"
msgstr "Das Umschreiben des Kopfs im Proxy"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:152
msgid ""
"The head is not forwarded verbatim. ``write_request_head`` "
"(``crates/net/src/request.rs``, crate ``sibuna-net``) re-emits the "
"request line and each header into the origin writer, dropping hop-by-hop "
"fields (``Connection``, ``Keep-Alive``, ``Proxy-Connection``, "
"``Transfer-Encoding``, ``TE``, ``Trailer``, ``Upgrade``, the proxy "
"authorization fields), any incoming forwarding or audit field "
"(``X-Forwarded-For``, ``X-Real-IP``, ``Forwarded``, "
"``X-Forwarded-Proto``, ``X-Forwarded-Host``, ``X-Forwarded-Port``, "
"``X-Sibuna-Status``, ``X-Sibuna-Rule``), ``Expect``, ``Content-Length``, "
"and every field the request's ``Connection`` header nominates. It then "
"appends the audit set. Body framing is generated, never copied:"
msgstr ""
"Der Kopf wird nicht wörtlich weitergeleitet. ``write_request_head`` "
"(``crates/net/src/request.rs``, Crate ``sibuna-net``) gibt die "
"Anfragezeile und jeden Header neu in den Writer zum Ursprungsserver aus "
"und lässt dabei weg: Hop-by-Hop-Felder (``Connection``, ``Keep-Alive``, "
"``Proxy-Connection``, ``Transfer-Encoding``, ``TE``, ``Trailer``, "
"``Upgrade``, die Felder der Proxy-Autorisierung), jedes eingehende "
"Weiterleitungs- oder Auditfeld (``X-Forwarded-For``, ``X-Real-IP``, "
"``Forwarded``, ``X-Forwarded-Proto``, ``X-Forwarded-Host``, "
"``X-Forwarded-Port``, ``X-Sibuna-Status``, ``X-Sibuna-Rule``), "
"``Expect``, ``Content-Length`` sowie jedes Feld, das der "
